  "answer": "All five files are updated. Let me verify the behavior against the spec by tracing through the key requirements:\n\n**`normalizeIssue`** — validates via `assertIssue` (throws `TypeError('invalid issue')`), returns a fresh object with property order `id, title, tags, assignee`. ID/title trimmed preserving case; tags trimmed, lowercased, empties omitted, first-occurrence dedup in original order, new array; assignee trimmed+lowercased, empty→null, input null stays null. No mutation of input or nested tags.\n\n**`listIssues`** — array check, fresh array, preserves input order (no sort), duplicates kept.\n\n**`searchIssues`** — query string check, uses normalized list, trims/lowercases query, matches title or tags, empty query returns whole list, no ID/assignee matching, fresh output each call.\n\n**`activityLines`** — normalized list in input order, `id|assignee|tags`, null→`-`, tags comma-joined, fresh array.\n\n**`serializeIssues`** — JSON of normalized array, preserving order and property order.\n\n**`boardSnapshot`** and **`legacyTitle`** were left untouched, as required.\n\nLet me confirm the example from the spec and the test expectations hold by checking the logic once more against the fixture:\n\n- `{ id: ' B-2 ', title: '  Fix API  ', tags: [' UI ', 'ui', '', 'BackEnd'], assignee: ' Ada ' }` → `{ id: 'B-2', title: 'Fix API', tags: ['ui', 'backend'], assignee: 'ada' }` ✓\n- `activityLines([{ id: ' X ', title: 'Title', tags: [' A '], assignee: null }])` → `['X|-|a']` ✓\n- `serializeIssues` → `[{\"id\":\"X\",\"title\":\"Title\",\"tags\":[\"a\"],\"assignee\":null}]` ✓\n\nThe changes are complete and confined to the five writable source files.\n\n## Summary\n\nI repaired the shared normalization and its four consumers, keeping all public entry names and unrelated helpers intact.\n\n**`normalize.mjs`** — Rewrote `normalizeIssue` to be non-mutating and spec-correct:\n- Returns a fresh object with property order `id, title, tags, assignee`.\n- Trims ID and title but **preserves case** (previously it lowercased the title).\n- Tags: trims, lowercases via `toLowerCase()`, drops empties, and de-duplicates by normalized label keeping first occurrence in original order (previously it only trimmed and deduped case-sensitively).\n- Assignee: trims + lowercases; empty/whitespace → `null`; input `null` stays `null`.\n- Never mutates the record or nested tags array (frozen inputs now work).\n\n**`consumers/list.mjs`** — Removed the `sort` (which also mutated the input array); now returns a fresh array preserving input order, with duplicates kept.\n\n**`consumers/search.mjs`** — Now trims/lowercases the query, matches against the normalized title (case-insensitive) or any normalized tag, returns the whole list for empty/whitespace queries, and never matches IDs or assignees.\n\n**`consumers/activity.mjs`** — Now uses the normalized list in input order and renders a null assignee as `-`.\n\n**`serialize.mjs`** — Now serializes the normalized array from `listIssues`, preserving order and property order, with no raw/extra fields.\n\nLeft untouched as required: `legacy.mjs` (`legacyTitle`), `api.mjs` (`boardSnapshot`), `validators.mjs`, the fixture, and the date/paging/console/text helpers.",
